# Transit Instruments — API keys (copy to `.env`; .env is gitignored, never commit it)
#
# All keys are OPTIONAL and SERVER-SIDE ONLY (the pipeline + serve.js read them via
# pipeline/lib/env.js). They are never shipped to the browser. The app degrades
# gracefully without them. No other data source needs a key — postcodes.io,
# CARTO/OSM tiles, londonbusroutes.net and the TfL tender pages are all keyless.

# ── TfL Unified API ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The authoritative London bus feed (routes, geometry, stops, live status, arrivals).
# Works key-less but is rate-limited; a subscription key raises the limit.
# Register + create a subscription, then copy the "Primary key":
#   https://api-portal.tfl.gov.uk/          (sign up / sign in)
#   https://api-portal.tfl.gov.uk/api-details   (subscribe → Profile → your keys)
#   https://api-portal.tfl.gov.uk/faq
# NOTE: the current portal issues a single subscription key (app_key). The old
# app_id + app_key pair is deprecated — just the one key is needed now.
TFL_APP_KEY=

# ── DVLA Vehicle Enquiry Service (VES) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Turns a bus registration (from TfL arrivals) into make / year / fuel / CO₂ —
# the basis for per-route avg fleet age + propulsion. Approval-gated (free).
# Apply for access, then copy the issued x-api-key:
#   https://developer-portal.driver-vehicle-licensing.api.gov.uk/
#   https://developer-portal.driver-vehicle-licensing.api.gov.uk/availableapis.html
#   https://developer-portal.driver-vehicle-licensing.api.gov.uk/apis/vehicle-enquiry-service/vehicle-enquiry-service-description.html
# Without it: live regs still work (TfL arrivals); only age/make enrichment skips.
DVLA_API_KEY=

# ── BODS — Bus Open Data Service (SIRI-VM) ───────────────────────────────────
# The authoritative LIVE VEHICLE POSITION feed (GPS lat/long, bearing, block/run
# and journey refs) — what powers Relay's live tracking. TfL's Unified API does
# NOT carry bus GPS (its predictions give next-stop + bearing only), so true
# positions come from here. Free registration; copy your API key:
#   https://data.bus-data.dft.gov.uk/          (Bus Open Data Service)
#   https://data.bus-data.dft.gov.uk/account/   (→ API key)
# Without it: Relay falls back to positions derived from TfL next-stop predictions.
BODS_API_KEY=

# ── Warehouse (historical API only) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Powers the /api/v1/history/* endpoints (time-series from the warehouse). The KEY
# is read server-side by the Pages Function (and serve.js in dev) — never the browser.
# Self-hosted Postgres + PostgREST (see README → "Historical API setup"). Use the
# anon-role key, NOT the service_role key, with RLS read policies on the history
# tables. Without these the live + current API groups still work; only
# /api/v1/history returns 503.
WAREHOUSE_URL=
WAREHOUSE_ANON_KEY=
